<description>
Extend a solid rectangle's color along outward diagonals after they pass through frame corners.
Input structure
The grid has a dominant background, one solid rectangular foreground object, and one one-cell-thick orthogonal frame object in a different color.
Rule
From each outer corner of the solid rectangle, trace the outward diagonal; if the first non-background pixel on that ray is a corner of the frame, continue past that frame pixel and paint every remaining background pixel on the same diagonal with the rectangle color.
Key insight
The frame corner selects which rectangle-corner diagonals are active, and the interior/background part of the ray before the frame is left unchanged.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "solid rectangular foreground object s",
  "path": "from each outer corner of s, follow the outward diagonal until the first non-background pixel; the ray is active only if that pixel is an orthogonal corner of the other-color frame, then continues on the same diagonal to the grid edge",
  "trajectory": "paint only the background pixels beyond the frame corner with s.color",
  "transform": "keep s, the frame, and the interior/background pixels before the frame unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 6-12 rows x 6-12 cols, always square [observed]
  colors: exactly 2 non-background colors; background is 0
  solid_rect:
    shape: 1-5 rows x 1-4 cols, fully filled with one color
    position: pushed into a corner of the frame's interior, touching the frame bbox boundary on all open sides
  frame:
    shape: L-shape (2 sides) or U-shape (3 sides) of a 3-7 x 4-6 bbox, 1-cell thick
    sides: 2-3 adjacent orthogonal sides of the bbox; open side(s) face a grid edge
    position: open side(s) flush with grid edge; solid rect + frame assembly occupies a corner/edge of the grid
    gap: exactly 1 empty row/col between solid rect and each present frame wall (so bbox gap = 2 counting the wall)
  rule: |
    From each outer corner of the solid rect, trace the outward diagonal. If the
    first non-bg pixel on that ray is a corner cell of the frame (has frame neighbors
    in both an orthogonal row and column), the ray is "active": paint every bg cell
    beyond that frame corner along the same diagonal to the grid edge with the solid rect's color.
  active_rays: 1-2 per example; L-frames produce 1, U-frames produce 2
  trail_length: 1-5 pixels per active ray; >=1 required (assert in solver)

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first (place frame+solid assembly, then verify trail space)
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size N x N (6-12), two distinct non-bg colors for solid and frame.
    2. Choose frame shape (L or U) and orientation (which corner of grid).
    3. Choose frame bbox dimensions (h 3-7, w 4-6) and solid rect dimensions fitting inside with gap=1 on each frame-wall side.
    4. Place the assembly at the chosen grid corner, open side(s) flush with grid edge.
    5. Verify each active corner's outward diagonal has >=1 bg cell beyond the frame corner before hitting the grid edge. If not, increase grid size or adjust.
    6. Input = grid with frame + solid rect. Output = input + painted diagonal trail pixels.
```
</generation_spec>
